        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "William Coooper",
                "firstName": "William",
                "lastName": "Coooper"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "Service providers claim that managed networks are essential to provide acceptable services. Meanwhile, new entrants are attempting to deliver broadband video services over the top of existing networks. Will faster networks address be sufficient to address quality of service?",
        "keywords": {}
    },
    {
        "publicationNumber": "4446773",
        "doi": null,
        "publicationYear": "2007",
        "publicationDate": "13-13 Dec. 2007",
        "articleNumber": "4451696",
        "articleTitle": "About the speaker",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "1",
        "endPage": "1",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "IET IPTV Conference 2007 - Deployment and Service Delivery",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Bill Scott",
                "firstName": "Bill",
                "lastName": "Scott"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "With content owners rushing to push their content at consumers and rapidly increasing consumer demand for internet video this session will look at who pays for the bandwidth, or, more accurately, the quality of service required to deliver it. If content is delivered over the top, is there an incentive for ISPs to invest in the infrastructure required? What business models will evolve to create a successful and perhaps more open market for broadband television?",
        "keywords": {}
    },
    {
        "publicationNumber": "4446773",
        "doi": null,
        "publicationYear": "2007",
        "publicationDate": "13-13 Dec. 2007",
        "articleNumber": "4451701",
        "articleTitle": "About the speaker",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "1",
        "endPage": "1",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "IET IPTV Conference 2007 - Deployment and Service Delivery",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "David Price",
                "firstName": "David",
                "lastName": "Price"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "IPTV is the provision of video programming targeted at a television display device using internet protocols to provide addressable delivery and has been widely adopted by DSL service providers around the world. How does this compete with other forms of “television”. It cannot and should not try to compete just on price and it cannot rely on an initial surge of subscribers that are disenchanted with their existing providers as these represent a limited market and form the section with the most churn. The magic ingredient has to be quality of service (in the truest sense) and choice of programming. This paper develops ideas based on the real life experience that Harmonic has gained with more than 40 leading IPTV service providers. It looks at the technological, commercial and legal challenges that must be tackled by any successful operator in this space.",
        "keywords": {}
    },
